--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI APIKeysPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state
holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable APIKeysDataSource
seam whose value types mirror the web `APIKey` 1:1 (production binds the KMP API-key
endpoints GET/POST /api-keys, DELETE /api-keys/{id}, POST /api-keys/{id}/revoke through
the seam). API-key metadata is control-plane data — it carries NO SI units, so there is
no unit conversion (the ADR display-boundary rule is N/A here, like the sibling Feature
Flags page). There are no charts and no map (manifest declares 0/0).

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the "Create Key"
header action) and BOTH web GlassPanels:

  GlassPanel1 — the one-time secret reveal: after a key is minted, the plaintext token
    is shown inside a frosted panel (TSGlassPanel) with a TSMaskedValue (click-to-reveal)
    and a TSCopyButton — web `<GlassPanel><MaskedValue/></GlassPanel>` + `<CopyButton/>`.
  GlassPanel2 — the per-key card: each key is a TSGlassPanel row with its key icon, name,
    permission chip (PermissionBadge: read→shield/green, read-write→shield/amber,
    admin→crown/power-purple #a855f7), an "Expired" badge + dimming for expired keys,
    the prefix / Created / Last used meta line, and trailing Revoke (hidden once expired)
    + Delete actions.

The create flow (web `Modal`) is an HIG-native sheet that swaps between the form
(Name TSTextField + Permissions TSSelect + Generate/Cancel) and the secret reveal, and
cannot be dismissed mid-create. The delete confirmation (web `ConfirmDialog`) is an
HIG-native sheet (title + the `{{name}}`-interpolated message + Cancel/Delete) that
stays open carrying the error on failure and cannot be dismissed mid-delete — faithful
to the web's keep-`deleteTarget`-on-failure semantics. The list switches its own data
state in place: loading (3 shimmer skeletons) / empty (ContentUnavailableView) /
error (+Retry) / success (the key rows) — never a blank region.

Adaptive across macOS/iPad (regular) + iPhone (compact): a ScrollView of cards that
reflow, ≥44pt icon-button tap targets on iOS, macOS pointer tooltips via `.help`,
VoiceOver labels/headers, Dynamic Type (token fonts), and light/dark via the P2 tokens.

Files (all new unless noted):
  Sources/Features/Admin/APIKeysModels.swift            (entry/permission/created/datasource/state/format)
  Sources/Features/Admin/APIKeysPageModel.swift         (@Observable model — list/create/delete/revoke)
  Sources/Features/Admin/APIKeysPageModel.Sample.swift  (actor seed source + real mutations)
  Sources/Features/Admin/APIKeysPage.swift              (view: header + list states + sheet wiring)
  Sources/Features/Admin/APIKeysPage.Row.swift          (key card GlassPanel2 + PermissionBadge)
  Sources/Features/Admin/APIKeysPage.CreateSheet.swift  (create form + GlassPanel1 reveal)
  Sources/Features/Admin/APIKeysPage.DeleteSheet.swift  (delete confirmation sheet)
  Sources/Features/Admin/APIKeysRouteRegistration.swift (.apiKeys route registration)
  Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/APIKeysPageModelTests.swift (24-case state-machine + format tests)
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift            (MOD: +.apiKeys case / pathSegment "api-keys" / icon / System group)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift            (MOD: wire APIKeysRouteRegistration as the outermost routeHosts base)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings    (MOD: +28 keys = 27 web parity literals + route.apiKeys)
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json         (MOD: +2 rows page:admin/APIKeys 32/32, apple-macos + apple-ios)

Navigation: the web route /api-keys maps 1:1 to AppRoute.apiKeys (pathSegment
"api-keys"), so AppRouteParser resolves it directly with NO alias needed (unlike the
/admin/* sibling pages). `.apiKeys` is added to the System sidebar group and is
reachable + deep-linkable. The only exhaustive AppRoute switches live in AppRoute.swift
(verified: `.featureFlags`/`.auditLog` are referenced only in AppRoute.swift +
AppRouteParser.swift + their own registrations), so no other file required editing.

i18n: every visible literal resolves from Localizable.xcstrings using the WEB key names
verbatim (the web page uses the English text AS the i18next key, e.g. t('API Keys'),
t('Create Key')), so the xcstrings keys are those literal strings. The `{{name}}` in
the delete message is the verbatim web key/default; the page resolves it via
String(localized:) + replacingOccurrences(of: "{{name}}", with: name) — the i18next
interpolation faithfully reproduced. Zero hardcoded user-facing strings.

